{%- comment -%}
  casa-reviews-ugc-v3.liquid — OctaMirror v3 ONLY copy of casa-reviews-ugc.liquid.
  The shared original is untouched; this copy carries the v3-specific settings.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Seoul Glow Lab — Reviews breakdown + community photo strip

  Paper-2 section. Aggregate score + 5-bar star distribution, then three
  quoted review cards, then a customer-photo strip.

  Per the Casa Design mirror-family PDP §05. The Judge.me widget stays
  where it is (bottom of the template) as the full, live review list —
  this section is the editorial summary that sits mid-page where the
  price objection actually lands.

  The rating, count and distribution are merchant-entered so they can be
  kept in sync with Judge.me by hand. They are NOT pulled live — if you
  change them here, change them in the buy-box star row too.

  The photo strip is product-scene imagery unless real customer photos
  are supplied. Do not label a product scene "customer photo" in the alt
  text — the per-block caption is the only claim made about it.

  Used by: templates/product.infinity-octamirror-v2.json
  Blocks:  review (quote, name, meta, stars) · photo (image, caption)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign reviews = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'review'
  assign photos = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'photo'

  comment
    Live fallback (additive, 2026-09-03): when the rating / count settings
    are left BLANK, read the store's review metafields instead — the same
    reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count pair Judge.me syncs and the
    JSON-LD already trusts — so the number can never drift from the widget
    at the bottom of the page. Typed settings still win, so every template
    that filled them in renders exactly as before.
  endcomment
  assign rating_src = s.rating
  if rating_src == blank and product.metafields.reviews.rating.value != blank
    assign rating_src = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating | round: 1
  endif
  assign count_src = s.review_count
  if count_src == blank and product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value != blank
    assign count_src = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value
  endif

  assign has_rating = false
  if rating_src != blank
    assign has_rating = true
  endif

  comment
    Normalise before any maths: `rating` is a text setting, so a merchant
    (or a localized admin) can type 4,7. "4,7" | round is 4 — one whole
    star short. Comma to dot first, then plus: 0 to force a number.
  endcomment
  assign rating_num = rating_src | append: '' | replace: ',', '.' | plus: 0

  comment
    Star fill is a percentage width over a 5-glyph track, NOT a rounded
    glyph count. `| round` turned 4.7 into five FULL stars next to the
    numeral 4.7 — the section contradicted itself and overstated the
    aggregate. Clamped so a typo'd 8 can't render eight stars.
  endcomment
  assign rating_clamped = rating_num
  if rating_clamped > 5
    assign rating_clamped = 5
  endif
  if rating_clamped < 0
    assign rating_clamped = 0
  endif
  assign rating_pct = rating_clamped | times: 20
-%}

<section
  id="casa-rug-{{ section.id }}"
  class="casa-rug{% if s.layout_density == 'one_frame' %} casa-rug--compact{% endif %}"
  style="
    --casa-rug-paper:   {{ s.color_paper   | default: '#F2F2EE' }};
    --casa-rug-card:    {{ s.color_card    | default: '#FAFAF7' }};
    --casa-rug-ink:     {{ s.color_ink     | default: '#0A0A0F' }};
    --casa-rug-purple:  {{ s.color_purple  | default: '#B0C3FA' }};
    --casa-rug-pink:    {{ s.color_pink    | default: '#5E0A02' }};
    --casa-rug-cyan:    {{ s.color_cyan    | default: '#F2FFA0' }};
    --casa-rug-pt:      {{ s.padding_top    | default: 96 }}px;
    --casa-rug-pb:      {{ s.padding_bottom | default: 96 }}px;
  "
>
  <div class="casa-rug__cap">
    <div class="casa-rug__head">
      <div class="casa-rug__summary">
        {%- if s.kicker != blank -%}
          <p class="casa-rug__mono casa-rug__mono--accent">{{ s.kicker | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="casa-rug__h2" id="casa-rug-h2-{{ section.id }}">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if has_rating -%}
          <div class="casa-rug__score">
            <span class="casa-rug__score-n">{{ rating_src }}</span>
            <span class="casa-rug__score-side">
              <span class="casa-rug__stars" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="casa-rug__stars-track">★★★★★</span>
                <span class="casa-rug__stars-fill" style="width: {{ rating_pct }}%;">★★★★★</span>
              </span>
              <span class="casa-rug__count">{{ rating_src }} {{ s.out_of_label | default: 'out of 5' | escape }}{% if count_src != blank %} — {{ count_src }} {{ s.count_label | default: 'verified reviews' | escape }}{% endif %}</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if s.dist_5 > 0 or s.dist_4 > 0 or s.dist_3 > 0 or s.dist_2 > 0 or s.dist_1 > 0 -%}
        <ul class="casa-rug__bars">
          {%- assign dist = s.dist_5 | append: ',' | append: s.dist_4 | append: ',' | append: s.dist_3 | append: ',' | append: s.dist_2 | append: ',' | append: s.dist_1 | split: ',' -%}
          {%- for pct in dist -%}
            {%- assign star_n = 5 | minus: forloop.index0 -%}
            <li class="casa-rug__bar">
              <span class="casa-rug__bar-lbl">{{ star_n }} ★</span>
              <span class="casa-rug__bar-track">
                <span class="casa-rug__bar-fill" style="width: {{ pct }}%;"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="casa-rug__bar-pct">{{ pct }}%</span>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      In one-frame mode the grid becomes a horizontal scroll rail on phones.
      The cards hold no interactive content, so without a focusable region
      a keyboard user can reach the first card and nothing else — the rail
      scrolls only by pointer. Same fix, and same trade, as the rail in
      casa-install-steps: the region is a labelled tab stop so arrow keys
      scroll it. Only added in one-frame mode, since the comfortable layout
      is a plain grid with nothing to scroll.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if reviews.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The rail stays a real list: a role="group" on the <ul> stripped the
        list semantics and orphaned every <li> (axe "listitem"). A focusable,
        labelled <ul> is still keyboard-scrollable.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="casa-rug__grid"{% if s.layout_density == 'one_frame' and s.heading != blank %} aria-labelledby="casa-rug-h2-{{ section.id }}" tabindex="0"{% endif %}>
        {%- for block in reviews -%}
          {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
          {%- assign b_stars = b.stars | default: 5 -%}
          <li class="casa-rug__card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="casa-rug__card-top">
              <span class="casa-rug__stars casa-rug__stars--sm">
                <span class="visually-hidden">{{ b_stars }} {{ s.stars_sr_label | default: 'out of 5 stars' }}</span>
                <span class="casa-rug__stars-track" aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span>
                <span class="casa-rug__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true" style="width: {{ b_stars | times: 20 }}%;">★★★★★</span>
              </span>
              {%- if b.badge != blank -%}
                <span class="casa-rug__verified">{{ b.badge | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            <blockquote class="casa-rug__quote">{{ b.quote | escape | newline_to_br }}</blockquote>
            <div class="casa-rug__meta">
              <strong>{{ b.name | escape }}</strong>
              {%- if b.meta != blank -%}<span>{{ b.meta | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if photos.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="casa-rug__ugc">
        <div class="casa-rug__ugc-head">
          {%- if s.ugc_kicker != blank -%}
            <p class="casa-rug__mono casa-rug__mono--dim" id="casa-rug-ugc-lbl-{{ section.id }}">{{ s.ugc_kicker | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.ugc_link_label != blank and s.ugc_link_url != blank -%}
            <a class="casa-rug__ugc-link" href="{{ s.ugc_link_url }}">{{ s.ugc_link_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <ul class="casa-rug__ugc-grid"{% if s.layout_density == 'one_frame' and s.ugc_kicker != blank %} aria-labelledby="casa-rug-ugc-lbl-{{ section.id }}" tabindex="0"{% endif %}>
          {%- for block in photos -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign p = block.settings
              assign p_alt = p.image.alt
              if p_alt == blank
                assign p_alt = p.caption
              endif
              if p_alt == blank
                assign p_alt = product.title
              endif
            -%}
            <li
              class="casa-rug__ugc-cell"
              style="--casa-rug-focus: {{ p.image_focus | default: 'center' }};"
              {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
            >
              {%- if p.image != blank -%}
                {{
                  p.image
                  | image_url: width: 800
                  | image_tag:
                    widths: '200, 300, 400, 600, 800',
                    sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 33vw, 18vw',
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    decoding: 'async',
                    alt: p_alt
                }}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if p.caption != blank -%}
                <span class="casa-rug__ugc-badge">{{ p.caption | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.casa-rug {
  background: var(--casa-rug-paper, #F2F2EE);
  padding: var(--casa-rug-pt, 96px) 0 var(--casa-rug-pb, 96px);
}
.casa-rug__cap {
  max-width: 1440px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px);
}
.casa-rug__mono {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
}
.casa-rug__mono--accent { color: var(--casa-rug-purple, #B0C3FA); }
.casa-rug__mono--dim { color: #525252; }

.casa-rug__head {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px);
  align-items: center;
  margin-bottom: clamp(36px, 4vw, 52px);
}
@media (max-width: 1023px) {
  .casa-rug__head { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; }
}

.casa-rug__h2 {
  font-family: var(--casa-pdp-h2-family);
  font-size: var(--casa-pdp-h2-size);
  font-weight: var(--casa-pdp-h2-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--casa-pdp-h2-tracking);
  line-height: var(--casa-pdp-h2-line);
  color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.casa-rug__h2 em {
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 800;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--casa-rug-purple, #B0C3FA), var(--casa-rug-pink, #5E0A02), var(--casa-rug-cyan, #F2FFA0));
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
  background-clip: text;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  color: transparent;
}
@media (max-width: 380px) {
  .casa-rug__h2 em { font-size: 1.02em; }
}

.casa-rug__score {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 14px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.casa-rug__score-n {
  font-family: var(--font-body--family);
  font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 68px);
  font-weight: 300;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
}
.casa-rug__score-side {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 4px;
  min-width: 0;
}
.casa-rug__stars {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  /* MUST hug the glyph track. This span is a child of a column flex
     container, so it gets blockified and stretched to the column width —
     measured 268px against a 100px track, which made the percentage fill
     resolve to 252px and cover all five stars at full opacity. The whole
     point of the fill is defeated unless the containing block IS the
     track. max-content survives any parent layout. */
  width: max-content;
  max-width: 100%;
  color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
  font-size: 18px;
  letter-spacing: 2px;
  line-height: 1;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.casa-rug__stars--sm { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
/* A percentage-width fill over a full-opacity track, so 4.7 reads as 4.7
   stars instead of being rounded up to five. Track and fill are the same
   five glyphs, so they align at any font size or letter-spacing. */
.casa-rug__stars-track { opacity: 0.22; }
.casa-rug__stars-fill {
  position: absolute;
  inset-block-start: 0;
  inset-inline-start: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.casa-rug__count {
  font-size: 14px;
  color: #525252;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.casa-rug__bars {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
}
.casa-rug__bar {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 36px minmax(0, 1fr) 42px;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 12px;
}
.casa-rug__bar-lbl { color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
.casa-rug__bar-pct { color: #525252; text-align: end; }
.casa-rug__bar-track {
  height: 6px;
  background: #E0E0DA;
  border-radius: 999px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.casa-rug__bar-fill {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  background: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
}

.casa-rug__grid {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
}
@media (max-width: 1023px) {
  .casa-rug__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .casa-rug__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
}
.casa-rug__card {
  border: 1px solid #E3E3DE;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 24px);
  background: var(--casa-rug-card, #FAFAF7);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 14px;
  min-width: 0;
}
.casa-rug__card-top {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.casa-rug__verified {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: #525252;
  border: 1px solid #E3E3DE;
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 3px 8px;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.casa-rug__quote {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
  margin: 0;
  flex: 1;
  text-wrap: pretty;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
.casa-rug__meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 3px;
  border-top: 1px solid #E3E3DE;
  padding-top: 14px;
}
.casa-rug__meta strong { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F); }
.casa-rug__meta span {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: #525252;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.casa-rug__ugc { margin-top: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px); }
.casa-rug__ugc-head {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 16px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
}
.casa-rug__ugc-head .casa-rug__mono { margin-bottom: 0; }
.casa-rug__ugc-link {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--casa-rug-purple, #B0C3FA);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
  min-height: 44px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
}
.casa-rug__ugc-grid {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  /* auto-fit, not a fixed 5: six photos at 1440px wrapped one orphan tile
     onto a second row. 160px floor keeps 5 or 6 tiles on one row. */
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
}
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .casa-rug__ugc-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 8px; }
}
.casa-rug__ugc-cell {
  position: relative;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  overflow: hidden;
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: var(--casa-rug-ink, #0A0A0F);
  min-width: 0;
}
.casa-rug__ugc-cell img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  /* Square 1:1 crop of a wide scene photo will cut the product out of
     frame on `center` — the "Three sizes" shot loses its outer two
     mirrors. Per-block focal point, per the scene-crop rule. */
  object-position: var(--casa-rug-focus, center);
  display: block;
  transition: transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1);
}
.casa-rug__ugc-cell:hover img { transform: scale(1.06); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .casa-rug__ugc-cell img { transition: none; }
  .casa-rug__ugc-cell:hover img { transform: none; }
}
.casa-rug__ugc-badge {
  position: absolute;
  inset-inline-start: 8px;
  inset-block-end: 8px;
  max-width: calc(100% - 16px);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  color: #fff;
  background: rgba(10,10,15,0.62);
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 3px 8px;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* ── One-frame density ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   Opt-in via the "Section height" setting. The section is tuned to fit
   a single viewport frame so the whole review argument is legible in
   one look instead of across three scroll gestures.

   The budget it is cut against is the USABLE frame, not innerHeight:
   the header group is sticky (80px mobile / 100px desktop), so a 800px
   desktop viewport only ever shows 700px of section.

   On phones the three review cards are the dominant cost — stacked they
   are ~600px on their own. Compact turns them into a scroll-snap rail so
   N cards cost the height of one, which is also the pattern a thumb
   already expects. The rail is a <ul>, so it stays a list for a screen
   reader and Tab still reaches every card.                            */
/* Keyboard focus ring for the focusable rail regions (keyboard-only). */
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__grid:focus-visible,
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-grid:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--casa-rug-purple, #B0C3FA);
  outline-offset: 4px;
  border-radius: 12px;
}
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__mono { margin-bottom: 10px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__head { margin-bottom: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px); }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__h2 { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__score-n { font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px); }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__count { font-size: 13px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__bars { gap: 5px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__card { padding: clamp(13px, 1.6vw, 17px); gap: 10px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__quote { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.45; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__meta { padding-top: 10px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc { margin-top: 16px; }
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-head { margin-bottom: 10px; }
/* Square cells are the single biggest block of desktop height in this
   section (5 across a 1440px cap ≈ 250px tall each). A 3:2 crop keeps
   the strip readable at roughly two-thirds the cost. */
.casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-cell { aspect-ratio: 2.6 / 1; }
/* Do NOT shrink this below 44px to buy height — it is a real link and the
   only route to the full review list. An earlier compact pass dropped it
   to 32px, which failed the tap-target minimum; the pixels come out of the
   photo strip instead, which costs nothing but crop. */

/* Short viewports: the summary block is the cost — an oversized score
   numeral above five distribution bars. Both compress rather than
   disappear; the bars still say what they said, quieter. Keyed off
   HEIGHT, since the constraint is vertical room, not width. */


@media (max-width: 1023px) {
  /* The head stacks to one column here, so the summary and the five
     distribution bars are additive rather than side by side — 266px
     measured on a 390px phone. */
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__head { margin-bottom: 12px; gap: 18px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__bars { gap: 3px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__bar { font-size: 11px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__h2 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
}

@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__grid {
    grid-template-columns: none;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: 78%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    /* Full-bleed rail: cancel the cap padding so the first card starts at
       the same optical margin as the heading and the last one can scroll
       clear of the right edge. */
    margin-inline: calc(-1 * clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px));
    padding-inline: clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px);
    padding-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__grid::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__card { scroll-snap-align: start; }
  /* The tallest card sets the rail height, so quotes of uneven length do
     not make the rail lurch as you swipe. */
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-grid {
    grid-template-columns: none;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: 42%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    margin-inline: calc(-1 * clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px));
    padding-inline: clamp(20px, 5vw, 64px);
  }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-grid::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-cell { scroll-snap-align: start; }
}

/* 790px, not 800: it has to catch a 768-tall landscape tablet, which
   the first attempt at 760 missed by eight pixels, without also firing
   on an 800-tall laptop that already fits and would only get smaller
   for nothing.

   Height tiers live LAST. They share specificity with the width
   queries above and only win on source order — placed earlier they
   silently lost, which is exactly what happened on the first pass. */
@media (max-height: 790px) {
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__score-n { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 32px); }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__bars { gap: 2px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__bar { font-size: 10px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__head { margin-bottom: 10px; gap: 12px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc { margin-top: 10px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__ugc-cell { aspect-ratio: 2.8 / 1; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__card { padding: 11px; gap: 8px; }
  .casa-rug--compact .casa-rug__quote { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

